ellyfish, then move on to three demons who have taken up prayer and look faintly embarrassed about it. I never found a true fish with legs. The nearest are the two bronze sea monsters and the ketos vase, which have scales, fins and clawed limbs, so read them as fish-adjacent.","artworks":[{"id":"aic:106638","source":"aic","nativeId":"106638","title":"And that Eyes without Heads Were Floating Like Mollusks, plate 13 of 24","artist":"Odilon Redon","date":"1896","imageThumb":"https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/34725c4e-679d-684d-6399-1887ca591c99/full/843,/0/default.jpg","imageHires":"https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/34725c4e-679d-684d-6399-1887ca591c99/full/1686,/0/default.jpg","license":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://www.artic.edu/artworks/106638","accession":"1920.1769","medium":"Lithograph in black on light gray China paper laid down on ivory wove paper","dims":{"width":2128,"height":2925},"color":{"h":42,"s":16,"l":45}},{"id":"aic:90316","source":"aic","nativeId":"90316","title":"Guardian Spirit of the Waters","artist":"Odilon Redon","date":"1878","imageThumb":"https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/d2905eaf-73c2-7796-5121-54600b4b2df4/full/843,/0/default.jpg","imageHires":"https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/d2905eaf-73c2-7796-5121-54600b4b2df4/full/1686,/0/default.jpg","license":"CC0","sourceUrl":"https://www.artic.edu/artworks/90316","accession":"1950.1428","medium":"Various charcoals, with touches of black chalk, stumping, erasing, incising, and subtractive sponge work, heightened with traces of white chalk, on cream wove paper altered to a golden tone","dims":{"width":1840,"height":2250},"color":{"h":30,"s":0,"l":34}},{"id":"aic:79347","source":"aic","nativeId":"79347","title":"The Misshapen Polyp Floated on the Shores, a Sort of Smiling and Hideous Cyclops, plate 3 of 8 from \"Les Origines\"","artist":"Odilon Redon","date":"1883","imageThumb":"https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/babeb325-2bc8-ed98-94b7-eed54d0537a6/full/843,/0/default.jpg","imageHires":"https://www.artic.edu/iiif/2/babeb325-2bc8